reverse-growth

The idea and the order of the steps (site, company and news, when it grew, search, ads, who talks about it, own
content channel by channel, loops, hiring, moves against the curve, the path, ten plays with prompts) follow
rea-growth by Superdesign Dev Pty Ltd (https://github.com/superdesigndev/treg, skills/rea-growth), licensed under the
Apache License 2.0 with additional terms. This skill is a rewrite: the instructions are written from scratch, the
data comes from context.dev and open public feeds instead of treg's vendors, and growth.py is new code. It is not
affiliated with or endorsed by Superdesign or treg.

Changes from the original: context.dev replaces every paid data vendor; the traffic curve is replaced by named public
stand-ins (brand searches, Wikipedia page views, news per month); keyword rankings and backlinks are
left to OpenSEO's own skills; reviews (G2, app stores) and an optional context.dev monitor step are added; sample
rules are adapted to the smaller public feeds.
